#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - OHOS musl declares POSIX getline in the
# default mode; legacy same-name definitions must be renamed
# Source package: blimps/3.9 path-update audit (B-2 CONFIRMED, wording revised)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-musl-posix-decl-conflict-rename-legacy
trigger_tool:           clang|musl|getline
phase:                  build
error_signature:        conflicting types for 'getline'|static declaration of 'getline' follows non-static|conflicting types for 'getdelim'

severity:               2
category:               platform-libc|declarations|posix|legacy-c
match_keywords:         musl, OHOS, getline, getdelim, POSIX.1-2008, conflicting types, declaration conflict, rename, strict ISO, -std=c11, legacy C
title:                  OHOS musl declares POSIX getline in the default mode without any feature macro: legacy same-name definitions must be renamed, not warning-downgraded (strict ISO mode hides the declaration)

root_cause:             OHOS musl stdio.h declares
                        `ssize_t getline(char**, size_t*, FILE*)` in the
                        default gnu mode without requiring any
                        feature-test macro; in strict ISO mode
                        (-std=c11) the declaration is hidden — measured:
                        the same legacy definition compiles and runs
                        exit=0 there. A legacy definition like
                        `int getline(char *s, int n, FILE *f)` therefore
                        collides with the default-mode declaration and
                        clang raises a hard error ("conflicting types
                        for 'getline'") that cannot be downgraded with
                        -Wno-error, so the private definition must be
                        renamed (or removed if uncalled). Evidence
                        anchored on OHOS probes only; no cross-libc
                        comparison claims.
affected_scope:         Any legacy C project that defines functions sharing
                        names with POSIX.1-2008 additions (getline,
                        getdelim, strlcpy, ...) when ported to OHOS;
                        blimps 3.9 util.c hit exactly this with an
                        uncalled private getline.
verification_cmd:       printf '#include <stdio.h>\nint getline(char*s,int n,FILE*f){return 0;}' | /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -xc - -c 2>&1 | grep -q "conflicting types for 'getline'" && printf '#include <stdio.h>\nint getline(char*s,int n,FILE*f){return 0;}' | /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -xc -std=c11 - -c && echo PROBE_OK

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           rename-legacy-definition
rec_description:        Rename the private definition (and its call
                        sites) out of the POSIX namespace. If it is
                        never called anywhere in the tree (blimps 3.9
                        util.c getline: sole reference is the
                        definition), renaming or deleting it is
                        zero-risk; otherwise keep the new name static if
                        file-local.
rec_command:            sed -i 's/\bgetline(/legacy_getline(/g' util.c  (word-boundary rename scoped to the owning file(s))
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      migrate-to-posix-getline
fallback_description:   If the function carries real functionality and
                        POSIX semantics are wanted, migrate its callers
                        to the libc getline/getdelim (char**, size_t*
                        interface) instead of keeping a same-name
                        private variant.
fallback_command:       ""
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          patch

fallback2_priority:     3
fallback2_approach:     strict-iso-probe-only
fallback2_description:  Compiling in strict ISO mode (-std=c11) hides the
                        POSIX declaration and the conflict disappears
                        (measured exit=0). Use it only as a probe /
                        diagnostic to confirm the mechanism; switching a
                        whole legacy codebase to strict-ISO std flags is
                        risky and NOT recommended as a porting fix.
fallback2_command:      clang -std=c11 -c file.c
fallback2_auto_fix:     false
fallback2_impl:         build-option

forbid_1_pattern:       -Wno-error=.*conflicting|no-error.*getline
forbid_1_reason:        "conflicting types" is a clang hard error, not a
                        warning: no -Wno-error flag can downgrade it, so
                        any recipe relying on that is dead on arrival.
forbid_1_consequence:   Build fails at the same TU regardless of the
                        flag; time wasted chasing a non-existent
                        downgrade path.

forbid_2_pattern:       #define getline|define\s+getline\(
forbid_2_reason:        Macro-izing getline cannot be made
                        self-consistent: the stdio.h declaration line
                        `ssize_t getline(char **, size_t *, FILE *)`
                        either stays (same conflict) or is rewritten by
                        the macro into the very conflict being avoided;
                        the legacy signature differs from the POSIX one.
forbid_2_consequence:   Compile errors move around unpredictably or the
                        libc declaration is silently corrupted for every
                        including TU.

principles:             P-PATCH-003, P-PATCH-002
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             [E093, E420, E081]
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-musl-posix-decl-conflict-rename-legacy.md
last_updated:           2026-09-05
source_event:           blimps/3.9 path-update audit: B-2 CONFIRMED with
                        two wording findings adopted (default-mode vs
                        unconditional phrasing; strict-ISO hidden
                        declaration probe added)
authors:                GoliWie
source_pr:
source_commit:          6a8410663e

metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.85
